worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_code_examples.js"
  ceiling 520
  rationale "Issue #1164 code-example decomposition, browser twin (R1164-11, JS-first doctrine). JavaScript twin of rust/src/code_example_knowledge.rs (decompose against the seed vocabulary and grammar registry, generalize across languages, recompose from the aligned example bodies, step records and Links Notation renderers), added 2026-10-07; growth is the ported decomposer, not silent regrowth. Re-baselined 333 to 339 on 2026-10-07 for R1164-9, the print prose relation (kind print_stdout) that lets a held-out language such as Pascal learn its output call from its documentation, mirrored from the native decomposer. Re-baselined 339 to 375 on 2026-10-07 for R1164-11, tryCodeExamplePageQuery: the supplied-page route that reaches the decomposer when the query line evidences the seed meaning code_example_decomposition_request, mirroring code_example_page_answer in rust/src/solver_handlers/page_query_text.rs, so data/parity/cross-runtime-synthesis.json carries a decomposition case both runtimes answer. Re-baselined 375 to 520 on 2026-10-07 for issue #1165 R1165-1: rediscoverDocumentedProgram, the browser twin of rediscover_from_documentation in rust/src/discovery_production_documentation.rs, reads data/seed/coding-documentation-captures.lino and the documentation_route of data/seed/program-cache-policy.lino, recomposes the captured example with the task output bound, verifies it by decomposing it again and against the language run contract, and writeProgramTemplate answers write_program from it before any stored template (the rust, go and kotlin hello_world templates of formal_ai_worker_12.js are retired)."
